invariant: INV-17
file: src/aead.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: open_one_pass returns 0 on a bad tag without the wipe of the n
  bytes it wrote, so the caller holds the plaintext of a forged
  ciphertext, which is that ciphertext XORed with the keystream of the
  nonce (docs/decisions.md 85). The verdict is still right.
  bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test requires zeros where the plaintext was after a
  changed tag. Only an x86-64 host object calls open_one_pass, so the
  script builds the binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
    if (ok == 0) {
        ct_wipe(pt, n);
        return 0;
--- new
    if (ok == 0) {
        return 0;
